  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Randy V\u00e1squez held them to one run in five innings, and the Padres clawed back from a first-inning deficit to take control by the fifth.",
    "what_this_means": "Trailing after four innings is where this team usually folds. Instead they scratched out three runs in the fifth. The kind of inning where a single lead becomes a two-run cushion and momentum flips from borrowed back to earned. V\u00e1squez did the hard part first, staying sharp enough to keep the deficit small. Manny Machado's home run in that fifth-inning burst was the separator. One swing that turned traffic into a lead they held. They left two runners on in the second and didn't capitalize. That miss mattered until the fifth arrived. Inconsistency is the story of this team: they don't score when they need to, then they do, then they don't again. This time, they scored when it mattered.",
    "what_to_watch": "STL brings Walker Buehler to Petco on Saturday. A pitcher working back from shoulder issues, making his early-season starts count in a division where one game is the margin between climbing and falling.",
